{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_lelita_photlibrary", "label": "Lelita's Photlibrary (App)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Romantic private web app for the couple Jeicob & Lelita built with Next.js + React + Tailwind + Framer Motion, designed to look beautiful on desktop and mobile."}, {"id": "readme_password_recovery_flow", "label": "Password Recovery Flow (SMTP/Webhook/Debug)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "6-digit code with 10-minute expiration stored in state.resetCodes. Delivery attempts in order: SMTP via Nodemailer, then RESET_EMAIL_WEBHOOK_URL webhook, then local debug mode returning the code \u2014 layered fallback so recovery works even without SMTP configured."}, {"id": "readme_cloudinary_upload_flow", "label": "Cloudinary Local File Upload Flow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frontend converts local file to Data URL and calls uploadFile action on /api/app; backend signs the upload with CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET and stores into CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_FOLDER/media or /chat folders; Cloudinary's secure_url is then saved into app state."}, {"id": "readme_mongodb_state_persistence", "label": "MongoDB Atlas State Persistence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Backend persists users, resetCodes, phrase, theme, media, letters and chat in MongoDB Atlas via the official mongodb driver (collection app_state, document singleton) because local file writes do not work in production on Vercel; data/state.json is only an initial seed."}, {"id": "readme_media_data_model", "label": "Recommended MongoDB Media Data Model", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Suggested 'media' collection with owner, description, resourceType, publicId, secureUrl, dimensions and timestamps. Recommended indexes: createdAt desc for fast feed, owner+createdAt for per-user history, text index on description for search, unique publicId to avoid duplicates."}, {"id": "readme_media_durability_practices", "label": "Media Durability Best Practices", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "So media never 'disappears': always use HTTPS secure_url, never delete from Cloudinary without archiving in MongoDB (and vice versa), enable Atlas backups, fixed folder scheme lelita/<year>/<month>, store public_id + resource_type to regenerate optimized URLs, visual onError fallback in UI, soft-delete via deletedAt before hard delete, periodic cron reconciliation job between MongoDB and Cloudinary."}, {"id": "readme_media_feed", "label": "Photo/Video Feed with Infinite Scroll", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Collage/diary style feed with tilted cards, infinite scroll, local file upload to Cloudinary, description search, and author-only description editing."}, {"id": "readme_chat", "label": "Couple Chat (Text + Media)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "readme_lightbox", "label": "Lightbox with Prev/Next Navigation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": 